00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:14,540
Intonation Reduced sounds are all those extra sounds created by an absence of lip,

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:19,360
tongue, jaw, and throat movement. They're a principal function of intonation and are

4
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:24,840
truly indicative of the American sound. Reduced sounds are valleys. American

5
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:29,420
intonation is made up of peaks and valleys, tops of staircases, and bottoms

6
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:34,920
of staircases. To have strong peaks, you'll have to develop deep valleys. These

7
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:38,880
deep valleys should be filled with all kinds of reduced vowels, one in

8
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:44,440
particular, the completely neutral schwa. Ignore spelling. Since you probably first

9
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:48,380
became acquainted with English through the printed word, this is going to be quite a

10
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:52,920
challenge. The position of a syllable is more important than spelling as an

11
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:57,860
indication of correct pronunciation. For example, the words photograph and

12
00:00:57,860 --> 00:01:02,840
photography each have two O's and an A. The first word is stressed on the first

13
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:08,660
syllable, so photograph sounds like photograph. The second word is stressed on

14
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:14,400
the second syllable, photography, so the word comes out photography. You can see

15
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:19,360
here that their spelling doesn't tell you how they sound. Word stress or intonation

16
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:25,340
will determine the pronunciation. Listening to words. Concentrate on hearing

17
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:30,460
the pure sounds, not trying to make the word fit a familiar spelling. Otherwise,

18
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:34,900
you'll be taking the long way around and giving yourself both a lot of extra work

19
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:40,980
and an accent. Syllables that are perched atop a peak or a staircase are strong

20
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:46,160
sounds. That is, they maintain their original pronunciation. On the other hand,

21
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:51,140
syllables that fall in the valleys or on a lower stair step are weak sounds, thus

22
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:56,620
they're reduced. Some vowels are reduced completely to schwas, a very relaxed

23
00:01:56,620 --> 00:02:01,640
sound, while others are only toned down. In the following exercises, we'll be

24
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:07,580
dealing with these toned-down sounds. In the introduction, read this first page IV,

